│ patch_description        │ The simulated annealing phase deliberately accepts worsening moves, but the current       │
│                          │ program outputs its final state rather than the best state encountered. With the initial  │
│                          │ temperature proportional to the current variance, this can discard a substantially better │
│                          │ greedy or intermediate partition before termination. Store the assignment whenever the    │
│                          │ estimated objective reaches a new minimum and output that best-known assignment. This is  │
│                          │ a zero-query change and preserves SA exploration while guaranteeing that annealing cannot │
│                          │ make the returned estimated partition worse than its initial greedy state.                │
