│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ direct_balance_feedback                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This approach avoids reconstructing numeric weights from fragile additive estimates.      │
│                          │ Instead, it uses comparisons in two stages:                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. It builds a small ordered pivot sample, classifies every item into weight quantile     │
│                          │ buckets, and uses the exponential-distribution prior to create coarse proxy weights.      │
│                          │ 2. It constructs an initial LPT-style partition from those proxies, then spends all       │
│                          │ remaining useful queries directly on the actual objective: comparing two bag totals,      │
│                          │ selecting an item from the heavier bag whose proxy weight is close to half the estimated  │
│                          │ discrepancy, and testing the resulting transfer with the balance.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Unlike the previous method, the final optimization decisions are validated against real   │
│                          │ group sums rather than inferred individual weights. This makes it much more robust to     │
│                          │ inaccurate weight reconstruction while still exploiting the known exponential input       │
│                          │ distribution for candidate selection.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
