│ patch_name               │ reserve_actual_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Reserve part of the query budget for a final, weight-exact local improvement phase. The   │
│                          │ existing method spends every query on noisy numerical weight reconstruction, then         │
│                          │ optimizes only that reconstruction. Instead, after the estimated simulated annealing      │
│                          │ phase selects its best partition, use the remaining balance queries directly on the       │
│                          │ candidate partition.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For two groups A and B, after identifying A as heavier, moving item x from A to B         │
│                          │ improves the true squared-sum objective exactly when sum(A)-w(x) > sum(B). This can be    │
│                          │ tested legally by comparing A without x against B. Thus accepted moves are guaranteed     │
│                          │ true-objective improvements, independently of estimation errors. The final result is      │
│                          │ therefore refined using actual balance information rather than solely estimated weights.  │
