│ patch_name               │ rank_binary_repair                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover retains the current program’s effective rank-sampling and direct           │
│                          │ balance-feedback approach, while replacing its single heuristic transfer choice with a    │
│                          │ monotone binary search over candidate item sizes.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Items are first classified against sorted random pivots. Instead of assigning every       │
│                          │ bucket a fixed percentile, the proxy weights are derived from observed bucket populations │
│                          │ and exponential order-statistic quantiles. This uses the information contained in how     │
│                          │ many items fall between consecutive pivots.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For repair, the algorithm compares two groups, identifies the heavier one, sorts its      │
│                          │ candidate items by estimated proxy weight, and binary-searches for the largest transfer   │
│                          │ that does not make the previously-heavy group lighter. This is a safer and more targeted  │
│                          │ version of local balancing: every committed transfer is verified to reduce the actual     │
│                          │ imbalance without crossing over. Remaining queries are still consumed exactly as          │
│                          │ required.                                                                                 │
